end=s.index('\n\nC.3:',begin)
s=s[:begin]+'''A.4: the elementary numerical-polynomial derivative fails integrality; coordinate finite differences fail simplicial naturality. A-016 excludes even noncommutative strict relative DGAs with the exact desired associated graded. A-017 gives the complete ordinary numerical Kähler associated graded by finite lattices, including torsion, and proves its cotangent-complex identification. A-021 excludes the filtered-circle comparison, A-022 excludes the naive cosimplicial candidate on a finite space, and A-023 classifies all filtered bilinear pairings of the prescribed numerical tails. A-024 excludes any strict or coherently R-linear realization retaining the specified first two exterior rows and the nonzero T-transgression. D-025 rules out every positive uniform connectivity shift of the derived-binomial candidate. D-026 constructs the weaker simplexwise total-derived lift and proves its shadow comparison, but also proves that it is not the actual all-weight PD cochain comparison, already for S¹.

The remaining A.4 gate is an actual all-X filtered, multiplicative numerical cochain lift with associated graded equal to the weighted PD cochains, allowed to change the exterior-row realization. It cannot be settled merely by the weaker total-derived equivalence or by replacing the specified coefficient modules without proof. A current finite-space approach studies all possible filtered rank-one R-modules deforming I_1 and I_2, and a torus product between them. This is an active approach, not a claimed classification.''' + s[end:]
